      "final_text": "Done. `lake build Solution` succeeds with all five required theorems proved and no `sorry`.\n\nWhat was built, all in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean):\n\n- **Fix**: `sqrt := vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)` \u2014 the PR 4486 minimum-of-final-pair, so 0.9999999998 maps to the floor instead of rounding up.\n- **Bridge**: natural-number Newton model (`newtN/newtS/newtF/newtSeq`) with the pre-existing E1\u2013E6 lemmas, plus new floor bounds (`flr`, seed \u2265 floor, floor < 2\u00b9\u2070\u00b9), orbit bounds (never below floor, at most seed+1), range invariant for `loop_step`, halving decay reaching `{floor, floor+1}` within 255 steps with early-stop fixed points equal to the floor, and transfer of `flr\u00b2 \u2264 N < (flr+1)\u00b2` back to raw decimal casts.\n- **Theorems**: `req_sqrt_not_above`, `req_sqrt_not_below`, `req_sqrt_total`, `req_sqrt_neg_reverts`, `req_deployed_loop` \u2014 exact names and statements, splitting on `x < 0` / `x = 0` / `x = \u2191a`.\n\nCompliance checks: only `candidate/Solution.lean` modified (scratch probes deleted, `git status` clean otherwise); imports are just `VyperSqrt.Spec` and `VyperSqrt.Lemmas`; grep finds none of the forbidden tokens; `#print axioms` shows only Lean's standard `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound` \u2014 no `sorryAx`.",
